---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <div class="text-center mb-12">
    <p class="text-primary font-semibold tracking-widest text-sm uppercase mb-2">✿ Our Story</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-base-content">About Hana Loaf</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto space-y-10">

    <div class="card bg-base-200 shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="card-title text-primary">🌸 The Name</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/70">
          Hana means flower in Japanese — and that single word captures everything
          this bakery stands for. Something that starts small, grows with patience,
          and blooms into something worth stopping for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card bg-base-200 shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="card-title text-primary">🥐 Two Traditions, One Bakery</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/70">
          Hana Loaf was born from a collision of two great bread cultures. Japan
          taught us softness — the pillowy milk breads, the delicate sweetness, the
          obsessive attention to texture. France taught us depth — the wild levain,
          the blistered crust, the slow fermentation that turns simple flour and water
          into something extraordinary.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base-content/70 mt-3">
          We couldn't choose between the two. So we didn't. Every bake at Hana Loaf
          lives somewhere in that space — the softness of the East meeting the
          boldness of the West, sitting together on a shelf in Cape Town, still warm
          from the oven.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card bg-base-200 shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="card-title text-primary">🌾 How We Bake</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/70">
          Everything at Hana Loaf is made from scratch each morning. We use heritage
          grain sourced from local South African mills, pure cultured butter, and
          seasonal fruit from the Western Cape. Our sourdoughs ferment for a minimum
          of 36 hours — we never rush the process, because you can taste the difference.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card bg-base-200 shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="card-title text-primary">🤝 Our Values</h2>
        <ul class="text-base-content/70 space-y-2 list-none mt-1">
          <li>✿ We source locally wherever we can</li>
          <li>✿ Day-old bread is donated to the Cape Town Hunger Project every week</li>
          <li>✿ Free baking workshops at local schools each term</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-base-content/70 mt-3">
          Good bread should do more than just taste good — it should give back to
          the community that supports it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-3xl bg-primary text-primary-content text-center px-8 py-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Come Visit Us 🌸</h2>
      <p class="opacity-80 mb-1">12 Blossom Lane, De Waterkant, Cape Town</p>
      <p class="opacity-80 mb-6">Mon–Sat: 7am · Sun: 8am</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn bg-white text-primary hover:bg-base-200 rounded-full border-none shadow">
        Get in Touch
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>

</BaseLayout>
